# Compiled binaries
/dashboard
/career-agent
/agent
career_agent_bin
# dashboard_bin was the name bug #461 gitignored, but nothing builds it any
# more: the dashboard is built as career_dashboard_bin, and cmd/dashboard's
# assistedApplicationCommand looks for a sibling career_assist_bin. Both were
# left untracked and showed up in every `git status` during the 2026-08-06
# acceptance trial, one rebuild away from riding along in a commit at 17MB and
# 19MB. Kept the old entry so an older local build stays ignored too.
dashboard_bin
career_dashboard_bin
career_assist_bin

Omni_CoverLetter.pdf

# Python bytecode and virtualenv from the nlp_service microservice.
# A venv created by python3 -m venv self-ignores via its own .gitignore, but
# that is a property of the tool's version, not something to rely on.
__pycache__/
nlp_service/venv/
.pytest_cache/

# cmd/modelbench's JSON reports (improvement #484). The tool never writes
# here by default -- this just makes the documented convention (-out
# benchmark_results/...) safe if someone follows it.
/benchmark_results/
tracker_bin
tracker.log
tracker_daemon.log
profile.yaml

# Ad-hoc verification cohorts written during live-batch runs (e.g.
# applied_urls_verify82.txt, a one-off 82-job list committed on purpose so an
# in-flight task could recover its cohort). These are real posting URLs from a
# personal job search -- runtime exhaust, not a fixture, and nothing in the
# codebase reads them once the task that produced them closes.
applied_urls_verify*.txt

# cmd/demo's compiled binary. Every other build output is ignored above; this
# one was not, and a 12MB ELF rode along in the 2026-08-12 portfolio-hardening
# commit. The documented way to run it is `go run ./cmd/demo`. Anchored so it
# cannot shadow the cmd/demo/ package directory.
/demo

# Local tooling and support bundles unpacked into the repo root (a downloaded
# gh release, zipped log bundles). Convenient to keep locally, never part of
# the repository.
/gh_*_linux_amd64/
/gh_*_linux_amd64.tar.gz
logs*.zip
